From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Linux apps that run in a terminal open in the
 Terminal

Apps whose desktop file says Terminal=true (vim since 16852.17.5, htop,
mc) did nothing from the launcher: nickel-appd launched them through
GLib, which looks for a terminal emulator, and NickelOS has none but
ChromeOS's Terminal ("Unable to find terminal required for application").
They now open in the Terminal, as Crostini's terminal apps do
(guest_os::launcher::LaunchApplication: the app's executable and the
files), which runs the command on the device instead of a prompt (0003).

---
diff --git a/chrome/browser/ash/crostini/crostini_util.cc b/chrome/browser/ash/crostini/crostini_util.cc
--- a/chrome/browser/ash/crostini/crostini_util.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ash/crostini/crostini_util.cc
@@ -234,6 +234,28 @@
   RecordAppLaunchHistogram(CrostiniAppLaunchAppType::kRegisteredApp);
   guest_os::GuestOsRegistryServiceFactory::GetForProfile(profile)->AppLaunched(
       app_id);
+
+  // Apps that run in a terminal (Terminal=true: vim, htop) open in the
+  // Terminal, as Crostini's do (guest_os::launcher::LaunchApplication), which
+  // runs the command instead of a prompt (Chrome 0003). nickel-appd would ask
+  // GLib for a terminal emulator, and NickelOS has none but the Terminal.
+  if (registration.Terminal()) {
+    std::vector<std::string> terminal_args = {
+        registration.ExecutableFileName()};
+    for (const auto& arg : args) {
+      if (const auto* url = std::get_if<storage::FileSystemURL>(&arg)) {
+        terminal_args.push_back(url->path().value());
+      } else {
+        terminal_args.push_back(std::get<std::string>(arg));
+      }
+    }
+    guest_os::LaunchTerminal(profile, display_id, registration.ToGuestId(),
+                             /*cwd=*/std::string(), terminal_args);
+    return OnApplicationLaunched(app_id, std::move(callback),
+                                 CrostiniResult::UNKNOWN_ERROR,
+                                 /*success=*/true, std::string());
+  }
+
